//? Title: Highway Networks: Coupled Gates and Carry Derivatives
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A deep transform stack can attenuate signals and their derivatives before it learns useful
features. Highway layers mix a learned transform with a learned carry path. We check the
complete input-dependent Jacobian, compare a controlled hundred-layer scalar stack, and train
a twenty-hidden-layer MNIST classifier using an explicit tensor Adam loop.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.3_residual_and_dense_families/highway_networks.cpp`.

> The method

A highway layer computes H=ReLU(x Wh+bh), T=sigmoid(x Wt+bt), and

$$
y=H\odot T+x\odot(1-T).
$$
\alttext(The transform gate and its complementary carry weight mix a learned transform with the input.)

The shapes match; a separate projection changes widths when necessary. Convolutional layers
use two same-channel SAME filters, and a 1×1 convolution agrees with dense per-position
mixing after identical weights are reshaped. H uses He-uniform weights; the gate uses
Glorot and a negative initial bias. Bias arguments initialize newly created leaves only:
calling the model again does not reset a fitted gate. Explicit T=0/1 fixtures recover the
identity/transform limits. Finite learned biases use sigmoid gates rather than a hard switch.

With a column-form Jacobian J[j,k]=d y_j/d x_k, all three terms matter:

$$
J=\operatorname{diag}(1-T)
+\operatorname{diag}(T\odot\mathbf{1}_{a_H>0})W_H^T
+\operatorname{diag}((H-x)\odot T\odot(1-T))W_T^T.
$$
\alttext(The input derivative contains carry, transform and input-dependent gate terms.)

The last term remains even if the transform is locally inactive. The worked input (.8,-.5)
uses Wh=((.7,-.2),(.3,.8)), bh=(.2,.1), Wt=((.4,-.1),(-.2,.3)), bt=(-1,-1), in row-major
order. It gives transform (.61,0) and gate logits (-.58,-1.23). Tensor autograd agrees with
the analytic matrix, including its off-diagonal entries. The 1×1 convolution agrees in values
and input Jacobian, and every learned parameter tensor has a finite derivative.

Negative gate bias favours carrying initially, but input-dependent gates do not guarantee an
identity derivative. To isolate attenuation, a separate scalar fixture fixes H(x)=.5x and
T=sigmoid(b) independent of x. One layer has gain g=1−.5sigmoid(b); at positive input one,
100 layers have response and input derivative g¹⁰⁰. Plain layers give .5¹⁰⁰; b=0 gives .75¹⁰⁰,
and b=−3 gives (1−.5sigmoid(−3))¹⁰⁰. Relative-error checks avoid treating tiny nonzero
signals as zero. These fixed filters are a diagnostic, not an empirical claim about trained gates.

A width-D dense highway layer learns 2(D²+D) scalars and costs O(ND²). A square k×k
convolutional layer with C channels learns 2(k²C²+C) and costs O(NHW k²C²). The MNIST
classifier explicitly flattens 28×28 images, applies a 784→50 plain ReLU projection, nineteen
50-wide highway layers with initial gate bias −2, then ten linear logits: 136660 scalars.
Projection/output use Glorot; internal transforms use He. Evaluation is deterministic, with
no BN state or dropout. The full architecture and all parameter gradients are checked.

The bounded dataset fit uses 512 fitting digits, 128 validation digits and 128 official-test
digits, ten epochs and batch 32. Adam(.001) minimizes mean cross entropy plus .0001/2 times
the sum of kernel squares. Validation NLL selects a parameter checkpoint before test evaluation.
Preprocessing stays in tensor reshape; pixels remain in [0,1]. Cached MNIST is required.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/highway_networks_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/highway_networks_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/highway_networks_concept.tikz > build/highway_networks_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/highway_networks_concept.svg build/highway_networks_concept.dvi > build/highway_networks_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
